{"title":"1967 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 9th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> 1967 in Yugoslavia. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a parallelogram with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e67527934e0557de487e6fdc23ea439b269b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0784975d4b8be997f4dfdeb77135b8ffc032bce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a927bca8ae82d40cc8f9705523132b10bf69b1ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is acute, prove that the four circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with centers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> cover the parallelogram if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6b3ece819aeabce6b8554cac996ebaba4ff143.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a\\leq \\cos \\alpha + \\sqrt{3} \\sin \\alpha .\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that if one and only one edge of a tetrahedron is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then its volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b3c29453586d0319c9d2666f84ecfec0edb89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 1/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be natural numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b3859b5aecf7b935e84b17f75676191288ab36f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> is a prime greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/f/41fdff2b62373622c2283bc12fdb1bca24390a6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_s = s(s + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that the product\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/7/3078becf49b899923443bcf0fad39d69bd906f6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(c_{m+1} - c_k)(c_{m+2}- c_k)\\cdots (c_{m+n}- c_k)\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"18\" />\nis divisible by the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f1a803a6807efdbe1aed8e5f260f9389ba048e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1 c_2\\cdots c_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/556cc158bc00acb1f2c3742d787b9e266cfc2727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0 B_0 C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b42d873c1494b7a0700cf53c8e567ebcce72330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 B_1 C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> be any two acute-angled triangles. Consider all triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> that are similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15dc14722a92ea5f3e0fadacb0050c7ebb2f2b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A_1 B_1 C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> (so that vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> correspond to vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively) and circumscribed about triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/556cc158bc00acb1f2c3742d787b9e266cfc2727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0 B_0 C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/71145755882ef0f1e12d10935523847f1692373e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />). Of all such possible triangles, determine the one with maximum area, and construct it.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Consider the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6e495e577567d0bf2fc9500b85479a987a2aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ c_n \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, where\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e301dc5b3128e196a440a4f3443202c0342cef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_1 = a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_8\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008e4c777bdc97f5181d05164e7dcb13fec37911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_2 = a_1^2 + a_2^2 + \\cdots + a_8^2\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce26e72ef1985f46ac9b2fedbe0879501540c94c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cdots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec977c95b4923c8820ecc2d595b587aec1b06b6b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[c_n = a_1^n + a_2^n + \\cdots + a_8^n\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/2/ce26e72ef1985f46ac9b2fedbe0879501540c94c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cdots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\nin which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087594ea26fa196b8e61bc20a36228270dc695f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ead075983f8dbfa721f00c28be967778b4a6677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are real numbers not all equal to zero. Suppose that an infinite number of terms of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6e495e577567d0bf2fc9500b85479a987a2aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ c_n \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> are equal to zero. Find all natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790f9e49e5031e603cbf2f35daa960d1a62bb96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_n = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a sports contest, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> medals awarded on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> successive days (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />). On the first day, one medal and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f4e9ccf77d551cda645e6a7d3c68c27dc1aea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> of the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c78c16fe53ddc169da833e13a405ce4988d487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> medals were awarded. On the second day, two medals and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f4e9ccf77d551cda645e6a7d3c68c27dc1aea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> of the now remaining medals were awarded; and so on. On the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-th and last day, the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> medals were awarded. How many days did the contest last, and how many medals were awarded altogether?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO\" title=\"1967 IMO\">1967 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1967\">IMO 1967 Problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO\" title=\"1967 IMO\">1967 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1966_IMO\" title=\"1966 IMO\">1966 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1967 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_IMO\" title=\"1968 IMO\">1968 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 330/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 836/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10298/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.873      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.873      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8277:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041902 and revision id 143749. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}